maya: Quick heads-up — I'm opening a small docs PR to standardize cursor resume examples across Python/TS/Go for streaming + retry behavior. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4212

alex: Thanks! Do we want to show exponential backoff + an idempotent resume token example? :thinking:

maya: Yes — goal is two concise patterns: 1) server-driven cursor resume (resume_token) with retry/backoff, 2) local buffering with at-most-once semantics. Keep snippets minimal and consistent across SDKs.

chris: I can paste a tiny fetchWithRetry helper for the TS sample I used earlier.

chris: ```ts
async function fetchWithRetry(fn, retries = 3) {
  let backoff = 200;
  for (let i = 0; i <= retries; i++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (e) {
      if (i === retries) throw e;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
      backoff *= 2;
    }
  }
}
```

maya: Perfect — for Python let's avoid adding tenacity as a dep; a small loop is fine. Keep the resume_token name identical across samples (use `resume_token`).

